Those "bad results" may be connected to skill. Daggers at unskilled aren't
very impressive, because you miss often. So start early, fight weak
monsters that won't harm you much with daggers, fend off the rest with
force bolt. That way you'll rapidly advance the skill to basic, where an
elven dagger becomes almost as effective as a quarterstaff.

The real advantage of daggers only begins to become clear when you have a
stack of them for multishot throwing at expert skill. Getting there
requires some work for a wizard, along with support from the pet to balance
out the inferior damage compared to the more convenient quarterstaff, but
it pays off.

